# `tools/rust/target/` is cargo's build directory. `configure` creates it during
# `R CMD INSTALL`, so it only exists here if a tarball is built from a tree that
# was already installed once — and it is hundreds of megabytes.
#
# `tools/rust/vendor/` is NOT excluded: when `.prepare` is run with GOG_VENDOR=1
# the vendored crates are the whole point, since CRAN forbids network during a
# build and the sources must travel.
^tools/rust/target$

# `.prepare` runs on the *cloned repository*, before `R CMD build` — so it has
# already done its work by the time a tarball exists and has no business being
# inside one. `R CMD check` flags it as a hidden file "most likely included in
# error", and that is right.
^\.prepare$
